<title>FRANCE: Algeria confirms 150,000-tonne durum tender.</title>
<headline>Algeria confirms 150,000-tonne durum tender.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>A senior Algerian official said on Tuesday Algeria had launched a snap tender to buy 150,000 tonnes of durum wheat between mid-March and the end of April.</p>
<p>The official from the Algerian Office Interprofessionnel des Cereales (OAIC) said Algeria would consider durum purchases from the United States, Canada and Syria -- &quot;our traditional market&quot;.</p>
<p>The tender calls for shipments of 50,000 tonnes over three periods -- March 16-31, April 1-15 and April 16-30.</p>
<p>European traders said on Monday that Algeria was seeking 150,000 tonnes of durum for mid-March to end-April shipment.</p>
</text>
